Z||000001||terryk||11-06-2001||09:46 PM||||Wait over-night and then check the fuel pressure. It could be leaking down overnight. <P>A weak coilpack usually shows up under load, but starting.<P>Next time, turn the key on, wait 10 seconds, then hit start. Does it fire immediately?||||reg||1
Z||000002||David DeVoe||11-07-2001||06:27 PM||||All else being ok the most common reason for hard starting (especially in cold weather) on a 3800 is a weak coil pak. Its an easy fix. Just changed one on my 88 Electra last winter. <BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-07-2001||07:09 PM||||Interesting. All of my coil-pak failures (or weakness) showed up under load but the engine started fine. Did the engine attempt to fire or just crank and crank then come to life? Also, are these the single 6 tower Maganavox or the 3 twin tower coils?<P>I'll watch for that in the future. Good data. <P>Let us know what you find.<P>Terry<P><BR>||||reg||1
